 estimated 620,000 residents, while the greater Research Triangle area has a population of over 2.37 million people. The city is located in the east-central part of the Piedmont region along the Eno River.","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Carolina_Theatre_%28Durham_Auditorium_1924%29.jpg/330px-Carolina_Theatre_%28Durham_Auditorium_1924%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Durham%2C_North_Carolina"},"twins":["Q2592","Q4301","Q204266"],"climate":{"temp":[3.4,5.2,9.5,15.2,20,24.7,26.7,25.8,22.2,16,9.7,5.7],"rain":[72,74,96,91,99,118,122,127,119,87,88,94],"cloud":[52,56,54,51,55,56,56,54,51,45,45,54]}}